	(text_box "DESIGN NOTES:\n- D4 for voltage protection for the IP chip\n- R5 because the INT logic voltage in unknown. Default disconnected before testing.\n- R13 pulldown so that the pin is not floating if diconnected via R5."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 212.598 17.526 0)
		(size 58.674 34.6177)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "039bb5a8-08d9-4c01-83fe-023704b5e96b")
	)
	(text_box "IP5306-I2C: MODIFICATIONS FROM MANUFACTURER'S EXAMPLE\n\n- The I2C bus (SCK & SDA lines) is pulled up to 3V3 as opposed to the manufacturer datasheet pulling it up to BATT+.\n- Added fuel gauge\n- Added Schottky to VOUT\n- Added 2N7000 to KEY button, can be pulled high to simulate a button press\n- Pulled INT to GND\n- Flashlight LED removed\n\nOTHER NOTES\n- VIN: The input voltage from a charger\n- VOUT: 5V boosted output"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.272 16.764 0)
		(size 58.674 34.6177)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7a661149-e32b-4b53-837b-36ff84233858")
	)
	(text_box "IP3005: MODIFICATIONS FROM MANUFACTURER'S EXAMPLE\n\n- P+, P-, designators by the manufacturer to label pack positive and negative. Distinctive from battery positive and negative."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.272 98.298 0)
		(size 58.674 22.35)
